  "$comment": "NPC combat definitions - server-side only. Each NPC's own entry (anims, sounds, `projectile`, `deathTicks`, `respawn`) is in npc-combat/: one file per NPC name or per piece of content, one NPC per line, and an id may appear in only one file. New content adds its own file there instead of editing a shared one. `projectile` is the projectile graphic id an npc's ranged/magic attack draws; without it the default generic arrow/magic projectile is used. `deathTicks` is how long the death animation plays before the death itself (drops, removal); 2 when absent. This file keeps the inferred `refs` rows (overridden by npc-combat/) and the fallback `defaults`.",
